= La bajada

The commanders gather in the dark the way they gather for a funeral, because in a sense it is one. The arithmetic on the ground floor of the war is no longer in dispute: the columns are thinning, the materiel is short, the Colonel's map of you thickens faster than you can burn it. Nobody in this room is a coward and nobody says the word *surrender*, but everyone has arrived, by their own road, at the same sentence — *this cannot be won the way it is being fought.*

And there is a way down that is not annihilation. It has different names in different years — the amnesty when Reyes Heroles opens it, a quiet dissolution back into the legal Movement when he does not, the columns walking out of the sierra in ones and twos to become organizers, teachers, the hard cadres of a political work that needs people who have already seen the worst. What comes down the mountain is not nothing. It is the war's whole harvest: the veterans, the legend, the southern networks, the map of who can be trusted with a life. A war that ends in the dark harvests none of it. A war that chooses its own ending keeps it all.

The alternative is to stay, and most who stay are, in the end, written into the memorial.

- @deponer_bajada: Come down — end the war on the Movement's terms, and carry its harvest to the political road.
- @seguir_bajada: Not yet. The mountain keeps its own, and the war is not over while a column still moves.

@deponer_bajada
on-arrival: {!
Q.via = "politica";
Q.descenso_hecho = 1;
Q.armada_entered = 0;
// the harvest: what the war made, walking down into the legal work
Q.veteranos = (Q.veteranos || 0) + 1;
var _harvest = Math.floor(((Q.pres_guerrero || 0) + (Q.pres_valle || 0) + (Q.pres_oaxaca || 0)) / 12);
Q.sup_peasants = (Q.sup_peasants || 0) + 3 + _harvest;
Q.sup_students = (Q.sup_students || 0) + 2;
Q.organizers = (Q.organizers || 0) + 1;
Q.unity = (Q.unity || 0) + 3;
// the milestone V of the sierra, earned by choosing the ending, if the war ever stood
if ((Q.pres_guerrero || 0) + (Q.pres_valle || 0) >= 30) { Q.sw_descenso = 1; Q.leyenda = (Q.leyenda || 0) + 1; }
// stand the war down: clear the danger clocks so the descent is not instantly re-punished
Q.moral_columnas = 60;
Q.coronel_red = Math.max(0, (Q.coronel_red || 0) - 30);
Q.represion = Math.max(40, (Q.represion || 0) - 10);
Q.postura_guerrilla = 2;
// but the stomach keeps what it digested: not everyone comes down
Q.members = Math.max(2, (Q.members || 0) - 1);
Q.expediente = Math.max(0, (Q.expediente || 0) - 6);
!}

They come down in ones and twos over a season, along roads chosen for having no memory, and the legal Movement absorbs them the way a body absorbs a long-held breath. Some do not come — the irreducibles who cannot imagine a life without the rifle, and the dead, who are past choosing — and their absence is its own wound. But the war did not end in a clearing at gunpoint. It ended in a decision, which is the only ending that leaves anything behind. The veterans take the hardest posts; the campo remembers who stood with it; the legend enters the songs, where no garrison can occupy it. You return to the political road smaller, older, and carrying something the road never had before: people who have already been to the end of the country and walked back.

